quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  21,102,They will not hear (even) its slightest murmur. And they will remain forever in what their souls desire.
  21,103,"The Greatest Horror will not disturb them, and the angels will greet them, (saying:) ‘This is your Day, which you were promised.’"
  21,104,"On that Day, We shall roll up the sky like the rolling of writing scrolls. As We began the first creation, so shall We bring it back—a promise (binding) upon Us. Indeed, We are going to do it."
  21,105,"And indeed, We wrote in al-Zabur (the Psalms) after the Reminder that My pious servants shall inherit the earth (in the Hereafter)."
  21,106,"There is, indeed, in this, a clear message (of achieving the objective) for a worshipful people."
  21,107,"And (Esteemed Prophet,) We did not send you but as a mercy for all (creatures of) the worlds."
  21,108,"Say: ‘It is revealed to me that your God is only One God. So, are you going to submit (to Him)?’"
  21,109,"But if they turn away, say: ‘I have proclaimed the message to you all equally. And I do not know (of my own accord) if what you have been promised is near or far."
  21,110,"Indeed, He knows whatever is spoken openly, and He knows whatever you conceal."
  21,111,And I do not know (of my own accord) if this (delaying of the punishment) is a trial for you and an enjoyment for a while.’
  21,112,"He (the Esteemed Prophet) said: ‘My Lord! Pass the true judgement! Our Lord is the Most-Compassionate, the One Whose help is sought against what you ascribe (to Him).’"
